#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124235 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "e1036a11-ebb3-594d-aba1-be259eb0596d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5419" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n11-9=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124236 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "4aa47a89-9f9b-55d8-ba01-a131b20e6c95" :question/math-academy-id "e-5421" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/62cc7238e6676b8a43d216ab6c8b30504602c68fd548832eceac9b710b885471.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/b85d717afa8af39d10517f909a09b53e6d379beef6e04e3d9ce7d3e48c88dca4.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/8e12a5386c3db2149324bd28c174a5410f7751e0c963cf80969e0cfdf14e5d7b.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124237 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/id #uuid "42d77ab8-0670-55bf-8b99-68270c8e5f2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5422" :question/problem "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/e20df1b44d2bfe100499eebfb4d2bdf8c1055978fdccbe11c8b5c0882052ace8.png) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "671144c3-db93-5744-ab20-b62fa3c4f1db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357545} {:answer/id #uuid "f23ce29b-039c-546e-9329-28b2901d1657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357546} {:answer/id #uuid "003892b2-4218-57e9-9770-b6e5240574c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357547} {:answer/id #uuid "e84b1d97-78f7-5217-a539-489c4b1b9e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357548} {:answer/id #uuid "2570bd07-3cbd-57bc-b023-e4380eb60101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e84b1d97-78f7-5217-a539-489c4b1b9e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357548} :answer-field/id #uuid "20286e89-3eb5-5fc8-ba79-3a7e0f584a2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4af574b7-0048-5ded-b921-a3f394b65c95" :question/math-academy-id "q-139969" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a matrix with $12$ columns and $4$ non-pivot columns, with enough rows for the $8$ required pivots ($m\\ge8$). What is $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)$?\n\nHint: Each non-pivot column corresponds to a free variable. Check that the required pivot count can fit in the number of rows." :question/worked-solution "Each non-pivot column corresponds to a free variable in $Bx=0$, so the null space has dimension equal to the number of non-pivot columns. There are $4$ such columns, hence $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)=4$.\n\nThe pivot count is $12-4=8$, so $\\operatorname{rank}(B)=8$. Rank-nullity confirms $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)=12-8=4$. A matrix with this rank must have at least $8$ rows. This is feasible for any row count $m\\ge8$; for example, put eight pivot columns and four zero columns in an $m\\times12$ matrix.\n\nThe original source specified a $7\\times12$ matrix with $4$ non-pivot columns. That would require $8$ pivots in only $7$ rows, contradicting $\\operatorname{rank}(B)\\le7$. No such original matrix exists. The corrected study question states the derived row requirement without choosing an arbitrary replacement row count. The original prompt, revealed answer $4$, worked solution and grade remain preserved as source evidence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddc47bb7-8399-5db0-805e-cf1a77bb9d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357552} {:answer/id #uuid "c33ce1ee-b9bd-5748-b8eb-fc3e7b4e54d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357553} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7d164b-c819-5a65-b58b-052528bd9dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357554} {:answer/id #uuid "740c55f9-4cdb-5f46-8d46-0ff436af82be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357555} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb5875d-0bec-597a-a6a1-f00c6814fd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c33ce1ee-b9bd-5748-b8eb-fc3e7b4e54d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357553} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd06cb3-5cfc-5b53-bbf8-06c449405e7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e6f5f29-58f7-5af1-9199-1be2bbe095af" :question/math-academy-id "q-139970" :question/problem "Let $W$ be a $9\\times 10$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $W?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(W))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $W.$ \n\nSince $W$ has $10$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $W$ is \n\n$$\n10-8=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(W))=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad726c4-d91a-5785-a1a7-d763ee50b0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357559} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6b8eb1-f17c-5ca5-b834-d3fd7e199fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357560} {:answer/id #uuid "0a248306-ad67-54c3-9125-c1aa57170b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357561} {:answer/id #uuid "2db0bffc-a16c-5a0e-ae1d-511d01092cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357562} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2c33a2-35b0-56fb-a111-44d380478cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ad726c4-d91a-5785-a1a7-d763ee50b0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357559} :answer-field/id #uuid "84a64eff-7cfc-507b-8add-eea710ce39ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ca98fa6-1d4d-5701-8042-4956f82e8b25" :question/math-academy-id "q-139973" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\,0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78ec2c6c-a5a5-5586-ae80-9c26e6999d3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357566} {:answer/id #uuid "921ea47d-d900-53e8-9f78-e67aaadc44f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357567} {:answer/id #uuid "5eea29ea-614b-5ad8-bed4-910e250f85ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357568} {:answer/id #uuid "a6716fa1-97cd-5529-80a9-2839358808b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357569} {:answer/id #uuid "a5093cfe-cca9-5375-ae9e-f4edfec27c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eea29ea-614b-5ad8-bed4-910e250f85ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357568} :answer-field/id #uuid "80275b54-09f7-5f1c-946b-aebd9645b6ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "492b31e9-b7e4-51e6-8ea7-a84a59b35cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-139975" :question/problem "If $W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(W)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))$, we reduce $W$ to row echelon form, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and  $1$\n non-pivot column (the $2$nd). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81e07bfb-c503-593d-b127-e0f5360ff1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121703} {:answer/id #uuid "d7469f89-bc79-5f32-9b31-5b252b4aa440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121704} {:answer/id #uuid "098ad1b8-464f-5181-9198-4030161af100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121705} {:answer/id #uuid "4460ff4e-3796-5628-adc9-b46e1e717138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121706} {:answer/id #uuid "56c36fe8-99cf-5aad-b8e7-9835640fb9c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56c36fe8-99cf-5aad-b8e7-9835640fb9c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121707} :answer-field/id #uuid "961747f3-07ef-5a2b-a1e6-a7732b196868" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "574853c6-277a-5d86-89c4-02f84dccc61a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34900" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a $8\\times 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(R))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $R.$ \n\nSince $R$ has $12$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $R$ is \n\n$$\n12-8=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(R))=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ace3e13f-28fe-5dcf-bc32-697235989c2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357573} {:answer/id #uuid "1473612f-f168-5523-8004-dc1450e5aa7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357574} {:answer/id #uuid "6379ccfa-77ce-5c87-b22e-f9f99eee93c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357575} {:answer/id #uuid "a76504d1-21c6-5294-87ea-cdae3b8f819f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357576} {:answer/id #uuid "77644b9c-7e2a-5491-9634-3a9763290884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77644b9c-7e2a-5491-9634-3a9763290884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357577} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a3e235-77cb-5f4e-8c7e-578443f99885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c48d63e4-4871-5ba2-a6bb-1f9bd1c16f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34902" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2ff973-9a9f-5fa2-b687-b3f523bddec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121709} {:answer/id #uuid "0048719e-d776-5014-807d-c9c9393a8a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121710} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8521fd-5f8e-5c34-bb4b-b7bde5e34659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121711} {:answer/id #uuid "342ffa45-3152-5bf1-8514-67d04d66cd62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121712} {:answer/id #uuid "5496060b-e37b-5226-a18c-f0ff352efd1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0048719e-d776-5014-807d-c9c9393a8a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121710} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b8df416-98ac-5bcb-9b06-d07198ce3853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f568aea-24ab-542a-9112-9bb117e4fc0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34904" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebdf3610-2c4c-54ed-add0-da03b389473d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357580} {:answer/id #uuid "964b69a5-399b-5c0d-8c8d-3cbbb0f4a697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357581} {:answer/id #uuid "c4122b5d-07c4-52ee-87a4-f8a6a94485bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357582} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2fd8dc-e8e1-5f34-840e-ff6b52a31678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357583} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1bc99f-f0da-58f1-bc78-d042294e4df4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4122b5d-07c4-52ee-87a4-f8a6a94485bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357582} :answer-field/id #uuid "31fa0fc6-a4f1-5f59-babb-dd28971d8c3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6d7f140-ace9-56e0-9a31-28b207bee64c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34906" :question/problem "Given $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91b02655-03b8-547c-b2f1-77d89dd1d869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357587} {:answer/id #uuid "974c4e8d-4562-5260-bbf5-b0e8b25be6ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357588} {:answer/id #uuid "092ac96f-feed-5ed9-b602-eb5a70972eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357589} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6ee3b3-c638-5140-bc16-7645baa5cf0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357590} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8d14bd-4216-5eab-8c92-6b8b9b1e2faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c6ee3b3-c638-5140-bc16-7645baa5cf0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357590} :answer-field/id #uuid "b30e2a8c-96b4-553f-9fdd-d8871ddf4cb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff42452d-01d4-5752-8070-c87c758d2102" :question/math-academy-id "q-34914" :question/problem "Given $Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))$, we reduce $Q$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $5$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61729448-1ee8-5e3d-b52c-0f9fa994f62e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357594} {:answer/id #uuid "37024cc8-7fe7-5adb-9316-c9d0ad181c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357595} {:answer/id #uuid "8abe3083-d820-525b-944e-f72134340cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357596} {:answer/id #uuid "15623246-a97b-5d83-b488-7eee83031445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357597} {:answer/id #uuid "7418d3e4-7734-5649-9a4b-01736d6df0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8abe3083-d820-525b-944e-f72134340cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357596} :answer-field/id #uuid "df00c518-3d37-53c3-a79f-f92ad322a04a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f8ebb94-16f5-552d-bf0b-134d3a592e8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34973" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c35de8aa-2abe-55d8-ad5c-ef33fe7c9cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357601} {:answer/id #uuid "c642972e-442b-5425-9397-0a3900f95fdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357602} {:answer/id #uuid "7169afc1-0bc9-5ee6-a3d1-bb236e492bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357603} {:answer/id #uuid "9f28a542-a321-5141-9c8b-aa2ee2855e8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357604} {:answer/id #uuid "42cb0e4a-8b56-5d2a-af1e-de4e4026243e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c642972e-442b-5425-9397-0a3900f95fdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357602} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b73c48-e741-5a54-b39b-bba3d9073122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f2681c7-5dcb-58a8-8f2c-8a6df1aae497" :question/math-academy-id "q-35316" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+1=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e132f54-8617-5b55-b47f-29490dedff3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357608} {:answer/id #uuid "4ddd7d86-cdc2-5a4c-af38-0c89230e6cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357609} {:answer/id #uuid "1bad2749-409f-5321-9d15-fd138559fab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357610} {:answer/id #uuid "18b2995c-979a-5d7c-85ed-6235e3f9b821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357611} {:answer/id #uuid "1dffed0e-f34f-5317-ac41-ab5549e33f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bad2749-409f-5321-9d15-fd138559fab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357610} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc2d0b23-6511-5c8e-8246-303d7b02dac2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0052961-15e8-52f8-a671-f43808d8e696" :question/math-academy-id "q-35317" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 9 & 28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-7){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 23 & 56\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b025c20a-e9f9-5dbd-b9c7-de5d82e83f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121775} {:answer/id #uuid "ea11f265-5d47-58c4-8760-6525e01f7e1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121776} {:answer/id #uuid "12e78a4d-1f27-5970-8ec7-66385d81a819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121777} {:answer/id #uuid "542d62ec-1ab8-5c32-ae78-45f3c5325d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121778} {:answer/id #uuid "58406b50-b737-5787-b805-91092173e368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12e78a4d-1f27-5970-8ec7-66385d81a819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121777} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd89b261-57fa-52e6-85cc-d9fadc9dcde5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a0b3d6d-593b-5e4e-ba8b-3eae5b6b11d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-35345" :question/problem "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(D)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))$, we reduce $D$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd70009-3e05-5ada-8af9-06e378d22a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123869} {:answer/id #uuid "229a8f40-911b-5f57-ae3f-13b7ab2fb464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123870} {:answer/id #uuid "2d47302e-cf87-5d2d-ad25-d716fd3f8913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123871} {:answer/id #uuid "407f6cef-a529-5ea5-8